\title{staggeredGMM: GMM Estimation of Treatment Effects Under Staggered Adoption}
\description{
Estimates cohort-by-time average treatment effects (CATTs) under staggered
treatment adoption by the generalized method of moments, following Arora
and Bijani (2026).
}
\details{
The single estimation entry point is \code{\link[=gmm_staggered]{gmm_staggered()}}. The
over-identification test of parallel trends and no anticipation is
\code{\link[=gmm_j_test]{gmm_j_test()}}.
}
\section{Data coding conventions}{

\code{gmm_staggered()} expects one row per unit-period. The cohort column gives
each unit's first treated period, with \code{0} reserved for units that are
never treated. Time must be integer-valued, and the set of periods present
in the data (pooled across units) must be consecutive. Individual units may
be missing individual periods; see \code{vignette("staggeredGMM")} for the
unbalanced-panel policy. Full details, including every condition that
raises an error, are in \code{\link[=gmm_staggered]{gmm_staggered()}}.
}

\references{
